==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Limited Stock}}

==Battleground==
*6 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*6 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*2 [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*3 [[Dagshund]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Razorback]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The main gimmick of this Otherworld Colosseum is a combination of two previous restrictions: a unit hardcap of 50, as well as setting all of your cats' recharge rate to a uniform number (16.67 seconds in this case). Any meatshield/tank you want to use here should be capable of taking a beating (e.g. [[Brainwashed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Eraser Cat]], [[Nono (Rare Cat)|Frolicking Nono CC]], [[Jetpack Cat (Rare Cat)|Jetpack Cat]]).

The restrictions make traditional [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] strats unviable for this stage, and necessitate the use of normally unorthodox crowd-controllers that benefit from these changes, such as [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] and [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]], to stop the Razorback in his tracks. Bombercat can still be utilized here, though much less effective than usual. Use [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] with a Defense UP (Sm) [[Cat Combo]] like [[Moby Dick (Combo)|Moby Dick]] to take care of the Dagshund at the start of the stage quickly, whilst stacking [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cats]], Cat Jobs, Sniper the Deadeyes, and any other viable DPS/crowd-controllers you may have at your disposal, including Talented [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Valkyrie Cat]] or [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]. Razorback should fall before long, making the cleanup phase a breeze.

